<Base title="Research & open source — Javad Khataei">
  <div class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Research & open source</span><h1>Questions worth<br />working on.</h1><p>Research into physical activity, tools for reproducible analysis, and selected projects.</p></div>
  <section class="split-section"><h2>Publication</h2><article><span class="eyebrow">First author · 2022</span><h2 class="paper-title">Predicting lying, sitting and walking at different intensities using smartphone accelerometers at three different wear locations: hands, pant pockets, backpack</h2><p class="paper-authors"><strong>Seyed Javad Khataeipour</strong>, Javad Rahimipour Anaraki, Arastoo Bozorgi, Machel Rayner, Fabien A Basset, and Daniel Fuller.</p><p class="meta">BMJ Open Sport & Exercise Medicine · May 9, 2022 · 8(2):e001242</p><div class="prose"><p>We evaluated machine learning methods for classifying activity type and intensity using smartphone accelerometers. Forty-eight participants carried phones in a hand, pocket, and backpack while completing activities in a laboratory.</p><p>Random forest models using raw accelerometer data achieved 92.9% accuracy for the right pocket, 89% for the right hand, and 90.8% for the backpack.</p></div><div class="paper-links"><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35601137/">PubMed ↗</a><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9086604/">Read the paper ↗</a><a href="https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjsem-2021-001242">DOI ↗</a></div><p class="quiet-note">Published under my full name, Seyed Javad Khataeipour.</p></article></section>
  <section class="split-section" id="open-source"><h2>Open source</h2><article class="record"><span class="eyebrow">R package · Co-author</span><h3 class="paper-title">activityCounts</h3><p>An open-source R package for generating ActiLife activity counts from raw accelerometer data across different device brands, supporting physical activity research.</p><div class="paper-links"><a href="https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=activityCounts">View on CRAN ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/walkabillylab/activityCounts">Source on GitHub ↗</a></div></article></section>
